fferent reposts  and stories and trying to make sense of  stuff and i thought it might be helpful  and make  somebody else feel not as isolated as i  was feeling and i didn't want people to  be grieving on their own as we all have  been  this past year so i'm so glad you posted  it  because i'm so glad that i get to be a  part of a show  that can pivot overnight and say i want  the privilege of speaking to my friend  ashley  and yet everyone on this planet  thanks to social media has a powerful  platform as well and when i see what you  did with yours  it is not often that something garners  millions of views overnight  what you did connected with people and  was utterly powerful  thanks true thank you and one i  i you know i said this to your team but  i  i first of all didn't expect for it to  go  viral in a sense at all and when you  reached out um out of everybody who kind  of reached out and wanted to  talk about the video talk about what i  said um i felt most comfortable coming  to you because it was  when i made that video it was to my  friends it was to my  the people in my life it was too um  really i mean to everyone but i felt so  comfortable being able to speak about it  because it is so personal still like  um and it's something that's still a  part of my identity and it's something  that i'm  reflecting on for the first time in my  life so  um thank you for being a safe space in  that way  i'm so glad what is your advice to  people  on what they can do right now  first of all and i talked about this in  the video i think that the thing that  everyone can do is think about what  they're saying  you know it starts with the president  who calls something the kung fu virus  something that is impacting the entire  world and it makes an enemy  of a certain group of people and to be  honest  when he said that even i  you know everyone in my life that i know  nobody was everyone kind of um  shook it off kind of thought oh that's  just something he's saying it